  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "u3NiwZmaElEhbRtByAtfuCsYEEU=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:00.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "## Connect is a host, not a UI skin\n\nConnect is the default host application Powerhouse ships. The distinction that matters: it does not reach across the network to a remote engine for its core behaviour \u2014 it **embeds** a Reactor and then adds three things the bare Reactor has no opinion about.\n\n- **A drives sidebar** \u2014 a file-browser-style view of every drive the user can reach.\n- **An editor host** \u2014 it inspects the document type being opened and mounts whichever editor is registered for it.\n- **A sync client** \u2014 it connects to Switchboard and replicates state in real time.\n\nBelow that line sits the Reactor: reducers, the deterministically ordered operation log, local storage. Above it sits Connect's own product surface. Nothing in the Reactor knows a sidebar exists.\n\n## Why the split is worth internalising\n\nIt localises bugs. A document whose state is wrong after an edit is a reducer problem \u2014 Reactor territory. A document that opens to a blank pane is an *editor-host* problem: the opened type has no registered editor, and the usual cause is a missing entry in `editors/editors.ts`.\n\n```ts\nimport type { EditorModule } from \"document-model\";\nimport { TodoListEditor } from \"./todo-list-editor/module.js\";\n\nexport const editors: EditorModule[] = [TodoListEditor];\n```\n\nIf that array is empty, Connect renders nothing when a todo document opens \u2014 even though the Reactor is holding a perfectly valid document with a complete history.\n\nConnect runs in two modes that are indistinguishable from an editor's point of view: **studio mode**, pointed at your local Reactor Package with reload-on-save, and **production mode**, a static bundle served from a host and talking to a production Switchboard. Same editor code, different environment. For local development you rarely wire any of this by hand \u2014 `ph vetra` brings up Connect, Switchboard, and MCP against your package automatically.\n\n_Source: apps/academy/docs/academy/02-Learn/05-connect/01-what-is-connect.mdx (Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45)._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T12:35:00.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:00.000Z"
    }
  },
